1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:07,762
He screamed "Wet the ropes!" when speaking meant death, right as a stone tower weighing three hundred and twenty tons was about to snap them in half.

2
00:00:07,712 --> 00:00:12,725
You see, the Pope is moving a giant Egyptian obelisk into the center of Rome.

3
00:00:12,725 --> 00:00:19,175
Eight hundred men are pulling on thick ropes, and to keep everyone focused, the Pope makes one terrifying rule.

4
00:00:19,175 --> 00:00:23,150
Speak a single word, and the hangman gets you on the spot.

5
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:26,225
For hours, the crowd is dead silent.

6
00:00:26,225 --> 00:00:30,900
Then, inches before the stone stands upright, the ropes stretch too far.

7
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:35,725
The tower stops moving, the hemp starts smoking, and it's about to crash down.

8
00:00:35,725 --> 00:00:40,500
Suddenly, an old sailor in the back screams, "Throw water on the ropes!

9
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:43,500
The guards grab him by the neck, laughing.

10
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:48,437
Great idea, sailor, let's make the ropes slippery so it crushes us faster.

11
00:00:48,437 --> 00:00:50,375
Wait, what?

12
00:00:50,375 --> 00:00:56,712
Well, the architect looks at the smoking ropes and tells his crew to dump barrels of water over every single one.

13
00:00:56,712 --> 00:01:00,262
You see, rope is made of twisted plant fibers.

14
00:01:00,262 --> 00:01:04,212
When those dry fibers drink up water, they swell sideways.

15
00:01:04,212 --> 00:01:09,462
And when a twisted rope puffs out sideways, it has to pull itself shorter lengthwise.

16
00:01:09,462 --> 00:01:16,200
As the water soaked in, the ropes shrank by inches, dragging three hundred and twenty tons of stone straight into place.

